      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T21:03:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Correct, the paragraph is referring to those two speed feature changes.\n\n- `sf-\u003ert_sf.hybrid_intra_pickmode \u003d 2` biases the encoder towards using the non-RD path more often by taking block variance into account. A value of 2 means that only blocks smaller than 16x16 with a variance of 101 or greater will go through the RD path.\n- `sf-\u003ert_sf.prune_palette_search_nonrd \u003d 1` reduces the palette search space in the non-RD path. A value of 1 is the mildest prune setting. During testing, I found the tradeoff worth it for images that have palette mode turned on by the screen detector (now that palette mode RDO is functional).\n\nDo you want me to add me this explanation somewhere else, or is leaving it as a CL comment good enough?",
      "parentUuid": "f528e75b_a8b7c912",
      "revId": "d8fba664d666e8b950d72cba0bde5f6d1a7d7028",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
