      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T21:03:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks Wan-Teh!\n\nFrom looking at the `subset1` efficiency curve chart (average file size vs QP level), speed 8 (after) images do tend to be overall a bit smaller than speed 7 images for the same QP level. The efficiency curve for speed 8 now solidly sits in between the speed 7 and speed 9 curves though (this used to not be the case before).\n\nFor my education: does libaom in general strive to produce larger files as speed increases? SVT-AV1 doesn\u0027t have this constraint.",
      "parentUuid": "5a1f63f5_0a486699",
      "revId": "d8fba664d666e8b950d72cba0bde5f6d1a7d7028",
