      "writtenOn": "2025-06-25T21:56:59Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the size issue goes back a few years that I struggled with for text to add to avifenc/libaom (which we did not add to the help). But in general this is what I settled on. quality 1-100: Higher quality at the cost of file size. effort 1-10: More encoding time, better compression ratio. We never added effort parameter. So I would think of it like this. speed 0-10: Faster speed, less encoding time, worse compression ratio. The nice thing about libaom is that for the quality/quantizer, the size vs quality is pretty monotonic. The speed is true as well for speeds 0-7, but speed 8-9 are usually much smaller than speed 7, which is we can\u0027t size speed at the code of size, we need to say somehting a little more ambiguous in speed at the cost of compression ratio.",
      "parentUuid": "9a38e5dd_41f20ad5",
      "revId": "d8fba664d666e8b950d72cba0bde5f6d1a7d7028",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
